<section id="S5.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.2 </span>Performance of Audio<math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>Text</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare Qwen3-Omni with other leading specialist and generalist models on ASR &amp; S2TT, voice-chatting, audio reasoning, and music understanding benchmarks. For brevity, we defer the results of the Qwen3-Omni-Thinking model on ASR &amp; S2TT and music understanding to the <span id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Appendix</span> <a href="#S9.SS1" title="9.1 More Evaluation on Speech and Music Understanding ‣ 9 Appendix ‣ Qwen3-Omni Technical Report" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="S5.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transcription performance for Audio<math id="S5.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>Text tasks (ASR &amp; S2TT), comparing Qwen3-Omni-Instruct with the baselines. The highest scores are shown in bold.</span></figcaption>
