</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.2 </span>Evaluation of Multilingual Speech Generation</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Qwen3-Omni supports speech generation across 10 languages. We evaluate its performance against both the MiniMax-Speech and ElevenLabs Multilingual v2 models for multilingual speech generation. As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T14" title="Table 14 ‣ 5.2.2 Evaluation of Multilingual Speech Generation ‣ 5.2 Evaluation of X→Speech ‣ 5 Evaluation ‣ Qwen3-Omni Technical Report" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, Qwen3-Omni surpasses these models by a significant margin for languages such as Chinese, English, and French, while delivering competitive results in the remaining languages. These findings indicate that Qwen3-Omni generates cloned speech with consistent stability and human-like voice across all evaluated languages.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span><span id="S5.T14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multilingual Speech Generation on MiniMax Multilingual Test Set. The highest scores are shown in bold.</span></figcaption>
